{"ts": "2026-10-26T22:06:56.928042Z", "run_id": "r-20261026T2206Z-46cf", "unit": "openspec:add-tenancy-foundation", "seq": 5, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-002", "target": "F-a449516e", "decision": "accept", "by": "delegate", "reason": "The finding is waived. The requirement \"The runtime role is unprivileged\" names a closed list of role conditions: missing, superuser, BYPASSRLS, owning a relation, or membership in ursitoare_owner or in a superuser or BYPASSRLS role. The checker implements exactly that list, and membership in pg_read_all_data or pg_write_all_data is not in it, which is why no scenario pins it down. The project assigns stray memberships of the app role to a different layer: the database specification requires ensureRoles to revoke every membership of the app role, and its repair scenario uses GRANT pg_read_all_data TO ursitoare_app as the very case that must be undone; roles.ts revokes each pg_auth_members row of the app role. The migration precondition and the health check use the same three membership conditions as the catalog checker, so the rule set is a deliberate project decision, not an omission of this unit. The judge's claim that has_table_privilege reports the predefined-role grant inconsisten", "text_sha256": "6c9c51fb7e60f2a6367d52698b372102570d702302817f2185ddf3e255d46aea", "answer_sha256": "055242f256df659350dd98a8e673d43278df9fae330a67cd0246c410b7f160c4", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code"}
